meta {
  name: 73 EMI Branch-Based Mapping E2E
  seq: 73
}

script:pre-request {
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // EMI Branch-Based Lab Adapter Mapping — full E2E, zero manual input.
  //
  // Proves the fix: LIS access (/emi/orders + /emi/submitResult) depends on the
  // branch CURRENTLY PROCESSING a test (LabReport.branchId, rehomed to follow the
  // specimen on an internal transfer), NOT the branch the order was created at.
  //
  // Two branches (a Collection Center + Branch A), one order created at the
  // Collection Center, and THREE adapters with different branch mappings:
  //   - adapterTokenCc   -> linked to Collection Center only
  //   - adapterTokenBa   -> linked to Branch A only
  //   - adapterTokenBoth -> linked to both
  // The same specimen barcode is scanned BEFORE (report at Collection Center) and
  // AFTER (report at Branch A) an internal transfer, giving all three cases:
  //   Case 1 (CC linked, BA not): works at CC, blocked at BA.
  //   Case 2 (BA linked, CC not): blocked at CC, works at BA.
  //   Case 3 (both linked):       works at CC and at BA.
  //
  // Run Folder, or click Next through 01..47. Every id/token is captured by each
  // request's post-response via bru.setVar(...) — nothing is copied by hand.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  if (!bru.getVar("baseUrl"))    bru.setVar("baseUrl", "http://localhost:3000/api/v1");
  // EMI endpoints live at the ROOT (not under /api/v1) — host only.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiBaseUrl")) bru.setVar("emiBaseUrl", "http://localhost:3000");

  // The seeded platform SiteAdmin (prisma/seed.ts) — the only credential assumed
  // to exist. Everything else (tenant, branches, users, catalogue) is created here.
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminEmail"))    bru.setVar("siteAdminEmail", "admin@kalnostics.com");
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("siteAdminPassword", "SuperSecret1");

  // Known passwords this flow sets, so every login is automated.
  if (!bru.getVar("operatorPassword"))       bru.setVar("operatorPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");
  if (!bru.getVar("bootstrapAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("bootstrapAdminPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");

  // The analyte the machine reports — equals the result parameter created on the
  // lab test (parameterCode), so the machine's universal_test_id matches it. Two
  // result values: one written BEFORE the transfer (at the Collection Center) and
  // one AFTER (at Branch A), so the final verifies prove which branch filled.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCode"))     bru.setVar("emiParamCode", "HGB");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnit"))     bru.setVar("emiParamUnit", "g/dL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueCc")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueCc", "13.5");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueBa")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueBa", "14.2");

  // One-time per-run unique suffix + derived unique mobiles (guarded: computed
  // once, reused for the whole run) so re-runs never collide on unique fields.
  if (!bru.getVar("tatRunId")) {
    const n = String(Date.now());
    bru.setVar("tatRunId", n.slice(-6));
    // 10-digit national mobiles (tenant create requires adminPhone ^\d{10}$).
    bru.setVar("adminBootstrapPhone", "95" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("ccOperatorMobile",    "98" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("baOperatorMobile",    "97" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("patientMobile",       "96" + n.slice(-8));
  }
}

docs {
  # EMI Branch-Based Lab Adapter Mapping — end-to-end

  Validates the branch-based LIS access rule from scratch: a Lab Adapter may only
  read/fill a test when the branch CURRENTLY PROCESSING that test is one the adapter
  is linked to. The processing branch is `LabReport.branchId`, which an internal
  transfer rehomes to follow the specimen — so it is the branch the test is worked
  at, not the branch the order was created at.

  ## Setup it builds
  - SiteAdmin, then tenant + business admin.
  - Two branches: a Collection Center (`ccBranchId`) and Branch A (`baBranchId`).
  - An operator at each branch with the accession permissions it needs
    (CC: collect/accept/send; BA: internal-referral pick-up/receive/accept).
  - The same lab test created in each branch's Master Data (same name/code, one
    `HGB` result parameter) and imported into each branch's list, so the two
    branches' BranchLabTest rows represent the same logical test (matched
    cross-branch by name/code).
  - One SiteAdmin equipment plus three adapters: `adapterTokenCc` (CC only),
    `adapterTokenBa` (BA only), `adapterTokenBoth` (both). All created
    `status: ONLINE` (required for live EMI auth).

  ## What it proves (one order at the Collection Center, scanned before and after an internal transfer)
  | Case | Adapter linked to | BEFORE transfer (report at CC) | AFTER transfer (report at Branch A) |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | 1 | Collection Center only | works (ut_ids populated, result filled) | blocked (ut_ids empty, nothing filled) |
  | 2 | Branch A only | blocked (ut_ids empty, nothing filled) | works (ut_ids populated, result filled) |
  | 3 | both | works | works |

  A blocked `GET /emi/orders` returns the legacy `{ "s": "200" }` envelope with an
  empty `ut_ids` (empty test list), not an error. A blocked submit returns
  `test_status: "no test match found for requested token"` with a per-report
  `fill_status` of "... not processed at a branch linked to this adapter".

  ## Verification
  Two report reads close the loop: after the before-phase, the report is read at the
  Collection Center (`source: ADAPTER`, `status: SAVED`, value = `emiResultValueCc`);
  after the after-phase, the same report is read at Branch A (`source: ADAPTER`,
  `status: SAVED`, value = `emiResultValueBa`) — proving the machine result landed
  at whichever branch was processing the test.

  ## Notes
  - EMI endpoints are at the root (`{{emiBaseUrl}}/emi/...`), authenticated by the
    `TOKEN` header (the adapter token), NOT the business JWT — see folder
    70 EMI Machine Interface for the standalone request reference.
  - Branch operating schedules are intentionally omitted (they drive TAT only; the
    EMI path does not depend on them).
}
